{
 "about": "What IS NOT NULL answers over resource['x'] and over the literal null. The PAP accepts both forms, and IS NULL over either is true whether x is there or not (dn-is-null-over-a-bracket-path, dn-is-null-over-the-null-literal), while == over resource['x'] ends the rule (df1). IS NOT NULL over them is recorded nowhere, so neither is whether it is a value or ends the rule. Each form is asked alone and through the probe and its control, with x present and absent; resource.a is y in every request, so the probe's right operand holds. The agent's condition parser accepts both conditions.",
 "resourceTypePrefix": "PARITY_SUITE_R10_",
 "pins": {},
